index 2dc4933d28..5746439dfb 100644
--- a/docs/tui.md
+++ b/docs/tui.md
@@ -19,6 +19,38 @@ The runtime has two layers:
 
 If your extension/tool can run headless, guard with `ctx.hasUI` / `pi.hasUI`. RPC can expose `hasUI === true` for protocol-backed dialogs while still not supporting `custom()`; `hasUI` alone does not guarantee a component can be mounted.
 
+### ACP-hosted native command UI
+
+ACP advertises `agentCapabilities._meta.commandUi = {version:1,protocol:"tsp"}`.
+Clients opt in by opening `_omp/ui/open` on a managed `sessionId` with `cols`,
+`rows`, `dark`, `reduceMotion` and optional supported `kinds`/`features`.
+The existing `InteractiveMode` uses that record's canonical `AgentSession`;
+Models, Settings and Resume keep their terminal controllers and persistence.
+The adapter never acquires stdin/stdout or a controlling terminal.
+
+| Extension | Input / result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `_omp/ui/open` | View geometry and appearance; opens or reconstructs the TSP document. |
+| `_omp/ui/event` | Native `event:TspEvent`, including frame credits and UTF-16 edits. |
+| `_omp/ui/input` | Keyboard `data`; optional `before` edit applies atomically before the keys. |
+| `_omp/ui/command` | Complete `text` submitted through the ordinary interactive command dispatcher. |
+| `_omp/ui/close` | Detaches the view, cancels its pending host services, retains the managed session. |
+| `_omp/ui/host_service_reply` (notification) | Single-use `serviceId`, `accepted`, optional `error`, with its original view origin. |
+
+`_omp/ui/message` notifications carry `{sessionId,transportId,message}`; `message`
+is the native TSP `{verb,body,headers?}` payload without terminal escape framing.
+`_omp/ui/state` publishes durable resume identity, cwd, streaming state and history
+replacement/restart transitions. Clients must reject stale transport generations.
+Closing one view does not terminate the ACP process or another managed session.
+
+Browser effects use `_omp/ui/host_service_request` and `_omp/ui/host_service_cancel`, not
+worker clipboard/open commands. Kinds are `copy_text`, `open_url`, and
+`open_stats_dashboard`; origin binds request, view and transport. Replies settle
+only the matching pending request. At most 32 services wait for 30 seconds; view
+close, disposal and timeout cancel them. Secret editors describe mask cells,
+never stored plaintext. Standard ACP tool/permission channels remain unchanged.
+
+
